est":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123276","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123276","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123276.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123276.patch","merged_at":"2026-09-30T16:57:13Z"},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nA ~year ago we decided to always assume trivial relocatability (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100509) since nontrivial relocatability is rarely useful, and not making the assumption is costly for core.\r\n\r\nHowever, well-meaning contributors might not be aware of this and try to fix code that is already correct (e.g. https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122627).\r\n\r\nThis PR attempts to prevent this by adding comments protecting the code.\r\nIt doubles as a reminder to people that trivial relocatability is assumed. This probably doesn't matter for us, but occasionally pops up in godot-cpp related chats.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nI also marked `SelfList` which is the only canonically nontrivially relocatable type in core.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_eve